# Financial Precision Standard

- Database Schema: Always enforce PostgreSQL `NUMERIC(14, 2)` across all financial and balance columns. Never use floating-point types (`REAL`, `FLOAT`, `DOUBLE`).
- Server Logic: Strictly calculate using `decimal.js` or string-based decimal logic in TypeScript. Never use native JavaScript math (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`) for money.
- Currency Formatting: Enforce 2-decimal formatted currency output (`Rs. 0.00`) across all ledger lines and invoice views.
